    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The essential point of Figure 6.2 is that two alleles can be identical by state, which means that they have the same sequence of nucleotides along the DNA, without being identical by descent. The concept of identity by descent pertains to the ancestral origin of an allele and not to its chemical makeup.",
