    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Wright, to the end of his long and extraordinarily productive life (he died in 1988 at the age of 98), always preferred his own interpretation of F as a correlation, because under some exceptional circumstances $ r_{UG} $ can be negative, and in these cases the probability interpretations fails because a probability cannot be negative.",
