    {
      "type": "answer",
      "content": "ANSWER The allele frequencies of A and a are estimated as $ (30 + 6)/70 = 0.514 $ and $ 1 - 0.514 = 0.486 $, respectively. The hypothesis is that F = 0.64, and so 1 - F = 0.36. The expected numbers of the genotypes AA, Aa, and aa are, respectively, $ [(0.514)^2(0.36) + (0.514)(0.64)](35) = 14.8 $, $ [2(0.514)(0.486)(0.36)](35) = 6.3 $, and $ [(0.486)^2(0.36) + (0.486)(0.64)](35) = 13.9 $. With these expectations, the $ \\chi^2 = 0.02 $ with one degree of freedom, and the associated probability is about 0.96. The fit to the inbreeding model is excellent.",
